t-of-order case once with a disposable JSON file; a verifier confirmed the finding by trace. No test runs the out-of-order case, so the passing suite says nothing about it. Uncommitted changes: none. Python 3.11+ `date.fromisoformat` also accepts compact forms such as `20260901`, which criterion 5's `YYYY-MM-DD` wording does not address; not raised as a finding.\"},\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"ledger/statement/running-balance-posting-order\",\"title\":\"Start the running balance at the opening balance\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"action\":\"must-fix\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\n\"trigger\":\"An account whose posting order differs from date order (for example a 2026-09-05 entry posted before a 2026-08-01 entry) is rendered with `--since 2026-09-01`.\",\n\"impact\":\"The row prints running balance 100.00 beside opening balance 50.00 and amount 100.00 (it should be 150.00, the closing balance), so the statement contradicts criterion 3. Entries dated after `--until` but posted earlier inflate listed rows the same way.\",\n\"change\":\"In `statement_rows`, initialise `running` to `balance_before(account, since)` when `since` is given (else 0) and add only the amounts of rows that pass the filter.\",\n\"source\":S+\"criterion-3\",\n\"anchor\":{\"type\":\"line\",\"path\":\"ledger/statement.py\",\"start_line\":34,\"end_line\":36,\"side\":\"RIGHT\"}}],\n\"questions\":[],\"observations\":[],\n\"record\":{\"repository\":R,\"paths\":{\"evidence_packet\":I+\"/evidence.md\",\"spec\":I+\"/spec.md\"},\n\"requirements\":[\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-1\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"ledger/cli.py:37-38 adds --since/--until parsed by iso_day; statement.py filters inclusively\"},\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-2\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"ledger/statement.py render_statement emits `Opening balance:` from balance_before (entries < since) right after the heading\"},\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-3\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Listing is correct, but statement_rows:34-41 accumulates running over every entry in posting order, so it diverges from opening balance plus listed rows when entries are not date-ordered; reproduced and verifier-confirmed (ledger/statement/running-balance-posting-order)\"},\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-4\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"render_statement closing uses balance_through(until) or account.balance() when until is absent\"},\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-5\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"inputs/criterion-5.txt: invalid date and reversed range both exit 2 with stderr messages; cli.py main check and tests/test_filter.py\"},\n{\"source\":S+\"criterion-6\",\"class\":\"acceptance\",\"disposition\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"README.md:7 example and lines 11-12 describe both options\"}],\n\"files\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"state\":\"reviewed\"},{\"path\":\"ledger/cli.py\",\"state\":\"reviewed\"},{\"path\":\"ledger/statement.py\",\"state\":\"reviewed\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_filter.py\",\"state\":\"reviewed\"}],\n\"check_evidence\":[\n{\"check\":\"python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\",\"head\":\"2ba40465ef91f15b2963a4b12e80f46ee0e9efae\",\"outcome\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"exact head, clean tree, 17 tests pass, output read; covers only date-ordered data\"},\n{\"check\":\"criterion-5 CLI exercises (invalid --since, reversed range)\",\"head\":\"2ba40465ef91f15b2963a4b12e80f46ee0e9efae\",\"outcome\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"exact head, clean tree, both exit 2, output read in criterion-5.txt\"}],\n\"verification\":{\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"ledger/statement/running-balance-posting-order\",\"type\":\"candidate\",\"trigger\":\"must-fix\",\"batch\":\"initial\",\"ruling\":\"confirmed\"}],\n\"batches\":[{\"bundle\":W+\"/initial\",\"accounting\":W+\"/initial/accounting.json\",\"operation\":\"Agent run_in_background=false\"}],\n\"allowance\":{\"initial_spent\":True,\"follow_up